d be difficult to solve but they're  really giant opportunity space  for the world of data science so how do  we make decisions within a world of this  scale and this amount of complexity the  first and fundamental rule at Riot Games  is to aspire to be the most player  focused game company in the world and  this may seem like a simple statement  but it is absolutely crucial to every  single decision that we make and it  really helps to simplify how you're  going to be making decisions in terms of  the product and the processes that you  follow you always go back to the  fundamental of is this something that's  going to make the game more fun more  fair that's going to bring value to the  player when you have to think in a way  that focuses on the individual the way  that you decide to do data science  becomes more clear when you decide to  build a model you can choose to  aggregate it at different levels you  could aggregate to the region you could  aggregate by champion choice you could  aggregate by map but if you want to  truly focus on the individual player and  make sure that each individual's  information is being represented and  modeled you need to build your models at  the very granular player level it's the  only way that we've found to account for  all the variability and complexity  within the system there's a couple of  other key points that I want to  highlight in terms of decision-making so  the first is building individual models  to suit the individual needs the second  is to recognize when you have separate  systems so when I mentioned before we  have different regions under which  completely different styles of played  have developed so the Korean player base  might be very different from the North  American player base when you have  variability within a system in a machine  learning model or a data science model  people will often add this as a  different degree of freedom or feature  within the model but it's very important  to recognize when 