ntroduced within this ecosystem well I  mentioned that a player has to pick one  individual champion we actually have  over a hundred and forty champions  that a player can pick from and each  individual one has a completely  different set of powers that are  available to a player when the person  chooses this individual champion they  will be playing with them from 20 to 50  minutes solid so going through all 140  plus would be a major time investment  for an individual play player another  and another source of complexity is that  we have major releases for the game  internationally every two weeks and what  I mean by major releases is that we can  release content we might release new  champions so if you think about this in  terms of sports  it's like introducing a new type of  player to the field and seeing what  happens for the game we introduce new  maps we have events these are major  changes to what is possible within the  space of the game and these patches and  releases have been happening every two  weeks almost since 2009 itself we also  release completely different Maps  so it's like you're changing the field  or the court in which the play is  happening and finally we have a fully  international game we are in many many  many different regions meaning we are  adding the complexity of culture and  different languages for any of our data  science problems that we would be  solving in addition each region like  Europe North America Latin America Korea  is on a completely different set of  servers which means that the community  and the style of play develops  independently within those individual  regions and then there's the numbers  themselves in terms of the players so we  have over 100 million monthly active  players over 500 billion data points per  day and petabytes and petabytes of data  so for those of you who are data  practitioners you can start to see what  all of this intricacy and complexity can  present in terms of not just things that  would be difficult to solve but they're  really giant opportunity space  for the world of data science so how do  we make decisions within a world of this  scale and this amount of complexity the  first and fundamental rule at Riot Games  is to aspire to be the most player  focused game company in the world and  this may seem like a simple statement  but it is absolutely crucial to every  single decision that we make and it  really helps to simplify how you're  going to be making decisions in terms of  the product and the processes that you  follow you always go back to the  fundamental of is this something that's  going to make the game more fun more  fair that's going to bring value to the  player when you have to think in a way  that focuses on the individual the way  that you decide to do data science  becomes more clear when you decide to  build a model you can choose to  aggregate it at different levels you  could aggregate to the region you could  aggregate by champion choice you could  aggregate by map but if you want to  truly focus on the individual player and  make sure that each individual's  information is being represented and  modeled you need to build your models at  the very granular player level it's the  only way that we've found to account for  all the variability and complexity  within the system there's a couple of  other key points that I want to  highlight in terms of decision-making so  the first is building individual models  to suit the individual needs the second  is to recognize when you have separate  systems so when I mentioned before we  have different regions under which  completely different styles of played  have developed so the Korean player base  might be very different from the North  American player base when you have  variability within a system in a machine  learning model or a data science model  people will often add this as a  different degree of freedom or feature  within the model but it's very important  to recognize when 