e bit about the data  science skills that come into play  Gamze this is not exhaustive and each  individual person doesn't need to know  all of these but you do need to build a  team that spans across this range of  knowledge so that you can solve the the  huge range of problems that are going to  be presented to you on a day to day  basis in terms of our stack we use a  pretty common stack we use Python of  course every single day or PI spark we  also use R for some of our modeling we  work on the data bricks platform right  games is an AWS or Amazon Web Services  shop and when we're doing business  visualizations and business analytics we  work with tableau so now I'll jump into  the fun stuff which is some of the  actual use cases that we've done at Riot  Games again this is not an exhaustive  list there is so much opportunity in the  space I'm not even going to mention  eSports info sack content none of that  is going to be necessarily what I'm  going to be talking about but there are  just massive spaces for this so the  first and a fundamental one is  understanding positional play so this is  another view of that map that I showed  before which has one lane across the  middle and two lanes across the side on  the top and on the bottom when a player  decides to join a game they join a  system where they're looking for a team  to be built for them so in this case  maybe someone said that they wanted to  play the middle position we will  automatically match them with the rest  of their team so that they find a  complete team composition when you do  that you need that assignment to be done  accurately and fast people don't want to  wait longer than 15 30 seconds to get  their team assignments so that they can  jump in and actually start playing the  game another point is we can  automatically detect how positions are  being used within the game so we can see  if we assign someone a particular  position do they follow through with  using that position how do they 